{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>His daughters and his sons' daughters.</b> Rashi explained: 'his sons' daughters' — this is Serach daughter of Asher and Jochebed daughter of Levi. And it is difficult: 'his sons' is fine, but 'his daughters' — who are they? For none of his daughters entered Egypt except Dinah, since the twin sisters died. And perhaps one may say that his daughters-in-law he calls 'his daughters.' But it is difficult to for me from what is written: 'all the souls of his sons and his daughters, thirty and three' — there one cannot say daughters-in-law, for they were not counted, as it is written: 'beside the wives of the sons of Jacob.' And perhaps he meant Dinah and Levi's daughter, and sons' daughters are like daughters. Thus it appears to me, and so it implies to one who understands from within Rashi's commentary."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:09.321633505Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}